# Line endings: always check out LF, on every OS.
#
# `make test` reads and writes the same CSV and factory data files on Linux,
# macOS and Windows, and the file format stores CRCs over the bytes.  A CRLF
# checkout on Windows (Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true) would
# make the committed examples differ from what the generators write, so the
# working tree is normalised to LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Factory data and assets: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.bin binary
*.sys binary
*.cal binary
*.diag binary

# Archives produced by the packaging scripts.
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.dmg binary
